---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ProductHeader from '../components/productHeader.astro';
import { arenaswapStores, productById } from '../lib/products';

const product = productById('arenaswap');

const steps = [
	'Open your streams. Pull up your games in separate tabs. ESPN+, Peacock, Paramount+, YouTube TV, Hulu, or any other browser-based stream works.',
	'Assign each tab once. Open the ArenaSwap popup, find each live game in the list, and connect it to its tab with a dropdown.',
	'Walk away. ArenaSwap scores every live game and switches you to the best one, checking as often as every 6 seconds when things get tense. The tab it picks is unmuted and the rest go quiet, so you hear the right broadcast.',
];

// The five components of the PowerScore, named the way the extension names them.
const signals = [
	'Closeness: how tight the score is, building as the game goes on.',
	'Late-game pressure: tension that rises through the final period of a close game, with a boost for a tie headed to overtime.',
	'Momentum: recent scoring runs, which spike and then fade.',
	'Lead changes: back-and-forth chaos.',
	'Comeback factor: teams climbing out of a hole.',
];
---

<Layout
	title="ArenaSwap · Lattice & Company"
	description="A browser extension that switches your tab to the most exciting live game."
>
	<div class:list={['px-3 py-5', product.accentClass]}>
		<div class="mx-auto" style="max-width: 48rem;">
			<ProductHeader
				product={product}
				title="Never miss the moment."
				lead="A free extension for Chrome, Firefox, and Edge."
				accentTail="moment."
				sans
			/>

			<p class="page-body">
				ArenaSwap watches every live game across 30+ sports leagues and automatically
				switches your browser tab to the most exciting one. Think NFL RedZone, but for every
				sport, every night, on whatever streaming service you already pay for.
			</p>

			<h2 class="arena-heading">How it works</h2>
			<ol class="page-list">
				{steps.map((s) => <li>{s}</li>)}
			</ol>

			<h2 class="arena-heading">The PowerScore</h2>
			<p class="page-body">
				Every live game gets a score out of 100, built from five signals.
			</p>
			<ul class="page-list">
				{signals.map((s) => <li>{s}</li>)}
			</ul>
			<p class="page-body">
				The signals stack and the total is capped at 100, so a genuinely exciting game climbs
				into the 80s and 90s while a blowout stays low. A frozen clock takes a penalty
				(halftime, timeouts, stoppages), which is what keeps you out of commercial breaks.
				Every card in the popup shows its score, and opening a game gives you the full
				breakdown: each signal live, the score over time, and what every component
				contributed.
			</p>

			<h2 class="arena-heading">Six sports, 30+ leagues</h2>
			<p class="page-body">
				Basketball, football, hockey, baseball, softball and soccer, from the NBA and the NFL
				to La Liga and the World Cup. Toggle any league off, and star your teams so their
				games score higher.
			</p>

			<h2 class="arena-heading">Tuned to you</h2>
			<p class="page-body">
				Sensitivity sets how big a scoring gap has to be before ArenaSwap moves. A cooldown
				keeps you from being tab-flipped mid-possession, and a switch delay covers a stream
				running behind the live data. Boost a game to hold it on screen, or pin one and it
				stays put. When everything on is a blowout, ArenaSwap can fall back to a standby tab:
				a pregame show, a highlights feed, whatever you keep in the background.
			</p>

			<h2 class="arena-heading">Private by default</h2>
			<p class="page-body">
				No account, no login, no subscription. No tracking, no analytics, no ads. Live scores
				come from ESPN's public API, and everything else runs in your browser. The full
				source, including the PowerScore package, is on GitHub.
			</p>

			<div class="d-flex flex-wrap align-items-center gap-4 mt-5">
				<a
					href="https://hiteacheryouare.github.io/arenaswap/"
					target="_blank"
					rel="noopener noreferrer"
					class="link-accent"
				>
					Get the extension <span aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span>
				</a>
				{
					arenaswapStores.map((s) => (
						<a href={s.href} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="link-quiet">
							{s.name}
						</a>
					))
				}
				<a
					href="https://github.com/hiteacheryouare/arenaswap"
					target="_blank"
					rel="noopener noreferrer"
					class="link-quiet"
				>
					GitHub
				</a>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</Layout>

<style>
	/* DM Sans Bold, like the h1 above it and like ArenaSwap's own site. The parent's serif
	   stops at the top of this page. */
	.arena-heading {
		font-family: 'DM Sans', system-ui, sans-serif;
		font-weight: 700;
		font-size: 1.375rem;
		letter-spacing: -0.02em;
		margin: 2.5rem 0 1rem;
	}
</style>
